{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "LUK.18.NLT"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/LUK/18-1391c9a8a0a2a317151e8b33af1f9319.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/LUK/18-1391c9a8a0a2a317151e8b33af1f9319.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}, {"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1668/32k/LUK/18-3c1304daa166bea8ebe9f15905f48ab8.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1668/m4a/32k/LUK/18-3c1304daa166bea8ebe9f15905f48ab8.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1668, "version_id": 59, "title": "Living Water Bible - ESV Music Project by Lutheran Bible Translators", "timing_available": false, "dramatized": true, "default": false}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bkLUK\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch18\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18\">\n            <div class=\"label\">18</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Parable of the Persistent Widow</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">And he told them a parable to the effect that they ought </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 21:36; Rom. 12:12; Eph. 6:18; Col. 4:2; 1 Thess. 5:17; [ch. 11:5-9] </span></span><span class=\"content\">always to pray and not </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Cor. 4:1, 16; 2 Thess. 3:13 (Gk.)</span></span><span class=\"content\">lose heart. </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"content\">He said, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;In a certain city there was a judge who </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[2 Cor. 8:21]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">neither feared God nor respected man.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">And there was a widow in that city who kept coming to him and saying, &#8216;Give me justice against my adversary.&#8217;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">For a while he refused, but afterward he said to himself, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 11:8]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8216;Though I neither fear God nor respect man,</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">yet because this widow keeps bothering me, I will give her justice, so that she will not beat me down by her continual coming.&#8217;&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"content\">And the Lord said, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Hear what the unrighteous judge says.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">And </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rev. 6:10; [Isa. 63:4] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">will not God give justice to </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 8:33; Col. 3:12; Titus 1:1; See Mark 13:20 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">his elect, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 88:1 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">who cry to him day and night? </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">James 5:7 (Gk.) </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Pet. 3:9</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Will he delay long over them?</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">I tell you, he will give justice to them </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Heb. 10:37 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">speedily. Nevertheless, when the Son of Man comes, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 17:26-30; [Matt. 24:12]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">will he find faith on earth?&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Pharisee and the Tax Collector</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">He also told this parable to some </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 16:15; [Matt. 5:20] </span></span><span class=\"content\">who trusted </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Cor. 1:9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">in themselves that they were righteous, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Prov. 30:12; Isa. 65:5; John 7:48, 49</span></span><span class=\"content\">and treated others with contempt: </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Two men </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">2 Kgs. 20:5, 8; Acts 3:1; [ver. 14]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">went up into the temple to pray, one a Pharisee and the other a tax collector.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">The Pharisee, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 6:5; Mark 11:25 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">standing by himself, prayed</span></span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">18:11 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">standing, prayed to himself</span></span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Rev. 3:17]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">thus: &#8216;God, I thank you that I am not like other men, extortioners, unjust, adulterers, or even like this tax collector.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 9:14 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">I fast twice a week; </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:42</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">I give tithes of all that I get.&#8217;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">But the tax collector, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 11 above] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">standing far off, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ezra 9:6 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">would not even lift up his eyes to heaven, but </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 23:48 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">beat his breast, saying, &#8216;God, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 79:9; Ezek. 16:63; Dan. 9:19</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">be merciful to me, a sinner!&#8217;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">I tell you, this man went down to his house justified, rather than the other. For </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 14:11</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but the one who humbles himself will be exalted.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Let the Children Come to Me</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.14\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 15-17, see Matt. 19:13-15; Mark 10:13-16   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Now they were bringing even infants to him that he might touch them. And when the disciples saw it, they </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 39</span></span><span class=\"content\">rebuked them. </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"content\">But Jesus called them to him, saying, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 18:3 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Let the children come to me, and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Mark 9:39]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">do not hinder them, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 18:3 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">for to such belongs the kingdom of God.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[John 3:3, 5] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Truly, I say to you, whoever does not </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 8:13; James 1:21]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">receive the kingdom of God like a child shall not enter it.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Rich Ruler</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.17\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 18-30, see Matt. 19:16-29; Mark 10:17-30; [ch. 10:25-28]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">And a ruler asked him, &#8220;Good Teacher, what must I do to </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Matt. 19:16]; See Matt. 25:34</span></span><span class=\"content\">inherit eternal life?&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.19\"><span class=\"label\">19</span><span class=\"content\">And Jesus said to him, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Why do you call me good? No one is good except God alone.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.20\"><span class=\"label\">20</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">You know the commandments: </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 13:9; Cited from Ex. 20:12-16; Deut. 5:16-20; [Matt. 5:21, 27]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8216;Do not commit adultery, Do not murder, Do not steal, Do not bear false witness, Honor your father and mother.&#8217;&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.21\"><span class=\"label\">21</span><span class=\"content\">And he said, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Phil. 3:6]</span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;All these I have kept from my youth.&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.22\"><span class=\"label\">22</span><span class=\"content\">When Jesus heard this, he said to him, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;One thing you still lack. </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:33; [ch. 16:9; 19:8; Acts 2:45; 4:34, 35; 1 Tim. 6:18, 19] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">Sell all that you have and distribute to the poor, and you will have </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 6:19, 20</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">treasure in heaven; and come, follow me.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.23\"><span class=\"label\">23</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ezek. 33:31]</span></span><span class=\"content\">But when he heard these things, he became very sad, for he was extremely rich. </span></span><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.24\"><span class=\"label\">24</span><span class=\"content\">Jesus, seeing that he had become sad, said, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[1 Cor. 1:26]; See Matt. 13:22 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;How difficult it is for those who have wealth to enter </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Matt. 12:28</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the kingdom of God!</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.25\"><span class=\"label\">25</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">For it is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle than for a rich person to enter </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 24 above]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the kingdom of God.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.26\"><span class=\"label\">26</span><span class=\"content\">Those who heard it said, &#8220;Then who can be saved?&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.27\"><span class=\"label\">27</span><span class=\"content\">But he said, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 1:37; Gen. 18:14; Job 42:2; Jer. 32:17, 27</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;What is impossible with man is possible with God.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.28\"><span class=\"label\">28</span><span class=\"content\">And Peter said, &#8220;See, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 4:20, 22; Mark 1:18, 20</span></span><span class=\"content\">we have left our homes and followed you.&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v29\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.29\"><span class=\"label\">29</span><span class=\"content\">And he said to them, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Truly, I say to you, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 14:26]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">there is no one who has left house or wife or brothers</span></span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">18:29 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">wife or brothers and sisters</span></span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">or parents or children, for the sake of the kingdom of God,</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.30\"><span class=\"label\">30</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">who will not receive </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Job 42:10] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">many times more </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Matt. 6:33] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">in this time, and in </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 12:32; Eph. 1:21; [ch. 20:35]</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the age to come eternal life.&#8221;</span></span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Jesus Foretells His Death a Third Time</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.30\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v31\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.31\"><span class=\"label\">31</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 31-33, see Matt. 20:17-19; Mark 10:32-34   </span></span><span class=\"content\">And taking the twelve, he said to them, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;See, </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 9:51 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">we are going up to Jerusalem, and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 22; See Matt. 1:22; 26:24</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">everything that is written about the Son of Man by the prophets will be accomplished.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v32\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.32\"><span class=\"label\">32</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">For he will be </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 27:2; John 18:30, 31; Acts 3:13; [Acts 2:23; 4:27; 21:11] </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">delivered over to the Gentiles and will be </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 27:26-31 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">mocked and shamefully treated and </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Mark 14:65; 15:19; See Matt. 26:67</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">spit upon.</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.33\"><span class=\"label\">33</span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">And after flogging him, they will kill him, and on </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 9:22</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">the third day he will rise.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.34\"><span class=\"label\">34</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Mark 9:32 </span></span><span class=\"content\">But they understood none of these things. </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 9:45; [ch. 24:16]</span></span><span class=\"content\">This saying was hidden from them, and they did not grasp what was said.</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Jesus Heals a Blind Beggar</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.34\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v35\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.35\"><span class=\"label\">35</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    For ver. 35-43, see Matt. 20:29-34; Mark 10:46-52   </span></span><span class=\"content\">As he drew near to Jericho, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 9:1, 8</span></span><span class=\"content\">a blind man was sitting by the roadside begging. </span></span><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.36\"><span class=\"label\">36</span><span class=\"content\">And hearing a crowd going by, he inquired what this meant. </span></span><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.37\"><span class=\"label\">37</span><span class=\"content\">They told him, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 2:23</span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Jesus of Nazareth is passing by.&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v38\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.38\"><span class=\"label\">38</span><span class=\"content\">And he cried out, &#8220;Jesus, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Matt. 1:1; 9:27</span></span><span class=\"content\">Son of David, have mercy on me!&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v39\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.39\"><span class=\"label\">39</span><span class=\"content\">And those who were in front </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 15</span></span><span class=\"content\">rebuked him, telling him to be silent. But he cried out all the more, &#8220;Son of David, have mercy on me!&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v40\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.40\"><span class=\"label\">40</span><span class=\"content\">And Jesus stopped and commanded him to be brought to him. And when he came near, he asked him, </span></span><span class=\"verse v41\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.41\"><span class=\"label\">41</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Mark 10:36</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;What do you want me to do for you?&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\"> He said, &#8220;Lord, let me recover my sight.&#8221; </span></span><span class=\"verse v42\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.42\"><span class=\"label\">42</span><span class=\"content\">And Jesus said to him, </span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">&#8220;Recover your sight; </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 7:50; 8:48; 17:19; Matt. 9:22; Mark 5:34 </span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">your faith has </span></span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 7:3; 8:36, 50</span></span><span class=\"wj\"><span class=\"content\">made you well.&#8221;</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v43\" data-usfm=\"LUK.18.43\"><span class=\"label\">43</span><span class=\"content\">And immediately he recovered his sight and followed him, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 7:16; 13:13 </span></span><span class=\"content\">glorifying God. And </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 19:37]</span></span><span class=\"content\">all the people, when they saw it, gave praise to God.</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["LUK.19"], "human": "Luke 19", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "previous": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["LUK.17"], "human": "Luke 17", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "reference": {"usfm": ["LUK.18"], "human": "Luke 18", "version_id": 59}}, "usfm": "LUK.18.NLT", "locale": "en", "versionData": {"audio": true, "copyright_short": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crosswa